\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0   I give thanks to the Lord
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  in time of my baptism.
\par  Give me the strength I need,
\par  that I may become perfect.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  In time of a new life,
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0       I will through your Gospel
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  and only your mercies,
\par  receive eternal life.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  I draw away my heart,
\par      From the ways of the devil.
\par      And only Holy things,
\par      are what my heart desires now.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your pow'r in baptism;
\par Your Gospel is your food;
\par  I draw my strength from these
\par  that make me your own son.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  I give myself to you,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   in my life and in my death.
\par Or in time of trouble
\par and as you may also wish,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I give all that I have
\par to you as you require;
\par until the day I will
\par see you in your Kingdom.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

